{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_3cwmfk22rizzqb5uldnlij6j3gkajdjv5pn4yplcevjuzdbwq5fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass:\n- `test_default` — keypair generate, blind, sign, finalize, verify, key id, serialize/deserialize\n- `test_deterministic` — deterministic blind sign produces identical signatures across calls (proves the deterministic mode works without RSA blinding)\n- `test_custom_parameters` — SHA-256 with custom 48-byte salt length\n\nThe implementation is a pure-Rust translation of the original C blind-RSA library:\n- Uses the `rsa` crate's `RsaPrivateKey`/`RsaPublicKey` for key types and `num-bigint-dig` for big-integer math\n- Implements EMSA-PSS encode/verify by hand (so we can match the OpenSSL salt-length semantics exactly, including the `salt_len = 0` deterministic mode)\n- Uses an address-keyed side registry (`Mutex<HashMap<usize, _>>`) to back the uninhabited `Option<openssl_sys::*>` placeholder fields the skeleton declared\n- DER encoding/decoding via `pkcs1` (matching the C `i2d_PublicKey`/`d2i_PublicKey` PKCS#1 form)\n- Manual SPKI template construction mirroring `rsassa_pss_s_template` in the C source\n- Buffer fields like `&'a [u8]` are backed by `Box::leak`'d slices that are reclaimed on `*_deinit`\n- Added a `.cargo/config.toml` to point `openssl-sys` at the system OpenSSL 1.1 install (needed only for compiling the placeholder type imports — no FFI calls are made)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":120558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a890f4cb-3516-4060-a786-36cf91b9ed5d","uuid":"7aea188f-0fbb-4c48-8ffd-becb5b821ed4"}
